Think penalty: while a request is inside its reasoning, subtract a fixed number of logits from
a few reflection-marker tokens ("Wait", "Hmm", "Alternatively"), on Model Runner V2 and under
speculative decoding (vLLM 0.28.0).

This is the THINK_PENALTY lever of the thinking-levers fork (single-user/start_qwen.sh,
docs/thinking-levers.md): the idea of NoWait (arXiv 2506.08343) applied at inference time,
without fine-tuning. It has to be a patch. Under speculative decoding vLLM rejects logit_bias
and custom logits processors, and bad_words would ban the words everywhere, code answers
included.

 - config/reasoning.py: `think_penalty` (logits; 0 = off, at most 100) and
   `think_penalty_words` on --reasoning-config. Each word, as written and with one leading
   space, must be a single ordinary token: not a special token, not a reasoning marker. The
   kept and dropped forms are logged. Nothing kept, a penalty without reasoning markers, or a
   value out of range refuses to start, and an unpatched vLLM rejects the keys outright.
 - config/vllm.py: refuses think_penalty on Model Runner V1, whose sampler this does not
   touch (SPEC=mtp runs V1; SPEC=dflash2 forces V2).
 - v1/worker/gpu/sample/thinking_budget.py: with the penalty on, a request without a
   thinking_token_budget gets one it can never reach (INT32_MAX). The existing marker tracking
   then runs for every request, and every new request resets its slot's marker cache, so a
   reused slot never carries the previous request's markers. A new kernel runs right after
   the budget kernels, one program per logits row: it repeats their draft-prefix marker scan
   and, if the row is inside reasoning, subtracts the penalty from the penalty tokens' logits.
   That is before temperature (the effect is penalty / T) and before top-k/top-p.

Every verify row goes through it, so speculative decoding stays exact with respect to the
penalized distribution; drafts are not penalized, which costs a little acceptance and no
correctness. A real thinking_token_budget still wins: it forces the end marker with a logit of
1e9. Nothing is penalized with thinking off, after </think>, in a raw completion without
markers, or in past turns, and with think_penalty 0 nothing runs. bench/test_think_penalty.py
checks it against a reference, in Triton's interpreter on the CPU and compiled on the GPU.

Author: Alex Woodka, 2026, for the thinking-levers fork of syv-ai/qwen38-27b-rtx3090. Applies to
vLLM 0.28.0 as the last line of patches/series and touches no file another patch touches.
Apache-2.0, like vLLM.

Apply from the repo root:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/think-penalty.patch

